      "id": "cve-2026-115560",
      "kind": "critical_flaw",
      "headline": "PHP patches four critical-rated flaws; session bug can lead to code execution",
      "summary": "PHP's maintainers patched four critical-rated flaws on 19 Nov in versions 8.2.36, 8.3.37, 8.4.28 and 8.5.13. The lead one, CVE-2026-115560, rated CVSS 9.2 by PHP, can let uploaded session data reach PHP's unserializer and lead to code execution. No source seen reports exploitation.",
