  "week_in_review": {
    "text": "The week mixed exploited-flaw news with AI claims. CISA added flaws in Cisco Expressway, Apache Roller, SAP NetWeaver and VMware vCenter to its exploited list, the last as a zero-day. Microsoft and Forescout each said AI models found new flaws. The measured picture was steady: the 26-week median days from disclosure to CISA listing was 15.5, with an 80% range of 12 to 20, against 21 in 2023–24.",
    "strongest_against": {
      "text": "The share of CISA-listed flaws already exploited at disclosure was 34% in the 26 weeks to 21 Nov, against 37% in 2023–24, with no clear change; this week's PHP flaws show no exploitation.",
      "claim_id": "SB-05",
      "source_ids": [
        "s7"
      ]
    },
    "from": "2026-11-16",
    "to": "2026-11-22",
    "table": [
